  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Elauwit’s core managed broadband and WiFi solutions are seeing strong underlying demand in multifamily, student, and senior living communities, as reflected in rapidly expanding contracted and billed units and a sizable project backlog. However, the revenue profile is inherently lumpy due to the timing of network construction projects; a decline in construction activity in the most recent quarter masked growth in recurring service revenue. The sales pipeline is building, with early verbal awards suggesting continued end-market momentum.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is scaling the sales organization, which is already converting pipeline into a stream of new commitments, while simultaneously implementing cost actions to restore construction gross margins toward targeted levels. Openly acknowledging the unevenness of project revenue, management is guiding the business toward a greater emphasis on recurring service income. The team’s focus remains on converting the growing backlog into activated units, signaling confidence in the long-term trajectory despite near-term fluctuations.",
